{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>You shall surely tithe all the produce of your seed, etc.</b> Since it is said (Malachi 3:10), ״הָבִיאוּ הַמַּעֲשֵׂר אֶל בֵּית הָאוֹצָר וְגוֹ׳ וַהֲרִיקוֹתִי לָכֶם בְּרָכָה עַד בְּלִי דָי״ — 'Bring the tithe into the storehouse… and I will pour out for you blessing without דַּי' — meaning that your lips will wear out from saying דַּי, 'enough' (Shabbat 32b). And the explanation of the matter is that there will be showered upon them an abundance of produce far beyond what is needed, and if so, surely they will not be able to say דַּי, for the expression ״דַּי״ is appropriate to say only when they have enough for what they lack; but when they have enough and more, they cannot say דַּי. And this is ״בְּלִי דָי״ — and ״בְּלִי״ means לֹא, 'not,' and He means to say that one will not say דַּי about it, and that is 'your lips will wear out from saying דַּי,' for the mouth cannot say דַּי when there is enough and more. And concerning that surpassing abundance He doubled ״עַשֵּׂר תְּעַשֵּׂר,״ meaning: if you ״עַשֵּׂר״ — give a tithe this year, ten from a hundred — then you will merit that for the coming year ״תְּעַשֵּׂר אֵת כָּל תְּבוּאַת זַרְעֶךָ״ of that year, and it will yield a thousand measures and you will give a hundred as tithe, and so it will do year after year — this is what it says: ״הַיֹּצֵא הַשָּׂדֶה שָׁנָה שָׁנָה״ (year by year)." "But since we find that all matters of charity are doubled: ״עַשֵּׂר תְּעַשֵּׂר,״ ״נָתוֹן תִּתֵּן,״ ״פָּתוֹחַ תִּפְתַּח,״ ״וְהַעֲבֵט תַּעֲבִיטֶנּוּ,״ and likewise the reward is doubled: ״כִּי בָּרֵךְ יְבָרֶכְךָ״ — therefore it appears that all matters of charity are doubled: the giving by hand, and the flattering by mouth, through not letting his heart grow resentful and giving him with a cheerful countenance and a whole heart, and the poor man hears no rebuke — as our Sages of blessed memory said (Berakhot 8a): one who prays should linger the measure of the entry of two doors, etc. — and this is to fulfill what is said (Psalms 17:15): ״אֲנִי בְּצֶדֶק אֶחֱזֶה פָנֶיךָ״ — 'I, in righteousness, will behold Your face.' And from here they learned that before one prays one should give a coin to charity (Bava Batra 10a), and this is the measure of two doors, as it is said: ״פָּתוֹחַ תִּפְתַּח אֶת יָדְךָ״ — opening of the hand and opening of the heart, which is mentioned in the preceding verse: ״לֹא תְאַמֵּץ אֶת לְבָבְךָ, וְלֹא תִקְפֹּץ אֶת יָדְךָ״. Therefore all matters of charity are doubled: one by hand and one by heart, and for each of these the Holy One, blessed be He, fixes a reward unto itself — therefore it says: ״כִּי בָּרֵךְ יְבָרֶכְךָ״. And concerning this our Sages of blessed memory said in the Midrash (Yalkut Shimoni, Isaiah 478): they sinned doubly, etc. — for they sinned in charity, whose nature is doubled, as it is written (Ezekiel 16:49): ״הִנֵּה זֶה הָיָה עֲוֹן סְדֹם אֲחוֹתֵךְ, יַד עָנִי וְאֶבְיוֹן לֹא הֶחֱזִיקָה״, and they sinned also in the Sabbaths, as it is written (ibid. 22:26): ״וּמִשַּׁבְּתוֹתַי הֶעְלִימוּ עֵינֵיהֶם״ — for all matters of Sabbath are doubled (Midrash Tehillim 92:1) — and they sinned also in the freeing of slaves in the days of Jeremiah (Jeremiah 34:11), and it is written concerning them (Deuteronomy 15:18): ״כִּי מִשְׁנֶה שְׂכַר שָׂכִיר עֲבָדְךָ״. And this is 'they sinned doubly,' etc." "Another matter: <b>All the doublings come to say</b> that if he gave once, he will merit to give also a second time, for giving draws on giving, and so with all of them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:13:33.259675445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}